{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1010419-pantheon-preview-the-teotl","id":1010419,"title":"Pantheon Preview: The Teotl","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-30T17:39:38-08:00","id":1010419,"title":"Pantheon Preview: The Teotl","content":"I figured <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sZhxhPlepq3wEawVoFNIrIaYzwtG-0_h5bUl9ujS_DY/edit\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> deserves its own thread, but I have to confess that I don't know enough about Aztec myth to say anything about it other than that it all seems very cool! I do have to question Tezcatlipoca's lack of a Beasts (Jaguar) Purview, but that could just be my own ignorance. I'm also a little sad to not yet see a &quot;thoughts on other Pantheons&quot; section, but I'm sure those will make it in. And is the multiple/plural Tezcatlipocas really a thing? I've never heard of it before.<br /> <br /> Discuss away!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 11-30-2016, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T18:03:59-08:00","id":1010434,"title":"","content":"I know pretty much nothing about the Teotl, but what I see here? I like. There's a LOT of options I had in mind for my Teotl-born Scion.<br /> <br /> Huehuecoyotl I'd never heard of, but in hindsight it's not surprising that the Aztecs would have a dedicated party God.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T18:07:58-08:00","id":1010435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1010419-pantheon-preview-the-teotl#post1010419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IAnd is the multiple/plural Tezcatlipocas really a thing? I've never heard of it before.Discuss away!</div> </div> </div> </div>Griff is the Aztec expert, but I do know the Tezcatlipoca thing is totally correct. There are Four Tezcatlipocas. One White, one Black, one Red, and one Blue IIRC. It's like a title for the rulers of the Pantheon. The Black Tezcatlipoca however we just call Tezcatlipoca, as his real name is... unknown. I don't know if it's a in-universe unknown, or something that's been lost to history.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T18:45:06-08:00","id":1010445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1010419-pantheon-preview-the-teotl?p=1010435#post1010435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Griff is the Aztec expert, but I do know the Tezcatlipoca thing is totally correct. There are Four Tezcatlipocas. One White, one Black, one Red, and one Blue IIRC. It's like a title for the rulers of the Pantheon. The Black Tezcatlipoca however we just call Tezcatlipoca, as his real name is... unknown. I don't know if it's a in-universe unknown, or something that's been lost to history.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#008000\">As I understand it, the </span>B\u200black Tezcatlipoca's<span style=\"color:#008000\"> true name MAY have been known, but was not spoken, for fear that he might hear it. </span><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Xipe Totec</span><span style=\"color:#008000\"> is the </span><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Red*,</span><span style=\"color:#ffffff\">Quetzalcoatl </span><span style=\"color:#008000\">is the </span><span style=\"color:#ffffff\">White</span><span style=\"color:#008000\">, and </span><span style=\"color:#0000ff\">Huitzilopochtli</span><span style=\"color:#008000\"> is the </span><span style=\"color:#0000ff\">Blue</span><span style=\"color:#008000\">, IIRC... </span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">\u200b<span style=\"font-size:9px\">*Please don't freak out, I'm not claiming to be a Mod.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 11-30-2016, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T18:51:15-08:00","id":1010451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1010419-pantheon-preview-the-teotl#post1010419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do have to question Tezcatlipoca's lack of a Beasts (Jaguar) Purview, but that could just be my own ignorance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man, how did I miss that. Fixed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T18:57:14-08:00","id":1010455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1010419-pantheon-preview-the-teotl?p=1010451#post1010451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh man, how did I miss that. Fixed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!<br /> <br /> Thankfully I don't know enough about any other Pantheon to cause a stink like I did over the Netjer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T20:22:44-08:00","id":1010470,"title":"","content":"Also, I have to say... I had expected a lot of the Nextlahualli Purview to be more related to gaining personal power from sacrifice, from how the Aztec PSP was portrayed in 1E. But I was pleasantly surprised to see that both the innate power and one of the Boons is about rewarding you for <i>paying back those who make offerings</i>. Which yes, makes sense... And it made me smile as I thought of the ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T21:13:36-08:00","id":1010485,"title":"","content":"So - will the Coyote of other Pantheons (say the Navajo Pantheon for example) be Huehuecoyotl getting around (like Yama does in Pantheons touched by Buddhism), possibly under other Mantles - or would those be other Coyotes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T21:19:01-08:00","id":1010488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1010419-pantheon-preview-the-teotl?p=1010485#post1010485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So - will the Coyote of other Pantheons (say the Navajo Pantheon for example) be Huehuecoyotl getting around (like Yama does in Pantheons touched by Buddhism), possibly under other Mantles - or would those be other Coyotes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be profoundly letdown if so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T21:21:58-08:00","id":1010489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1010419-pantheon-preview-the-teotl?p=1010485#post1010485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So - will the Coyote of other Pantheons (say the Navajo Pantheon for example) be Huehuecoyotl getting around (like Yama does in Pantheons touched by Buddhism), possibly under other Mantles - or would those be other Coyotes?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;They're my brothers. And me. And not me. And my kids.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;... Huehuecoyotl...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I got <b>REALLY </b>drunk.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You're ALWAYS drunk!&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T21:23:09-08:00","id":1010490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1010419-pantheon-preview-the-teotl?p=1010488#post1010488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would be profoundly letdown if so.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know, I'm open to the Old Man having found his way around all over western North America. It would definitely call for different Mantles in several cases though.<br /> <br /> (note: If he should have Beasts [Coyotes] he currently does not)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T21:31:15-08:00","id":1010499,"title":"","content":"I am a happy man at this point. My only teeny complaint is the lack of Tlazolteotl - she was a fairly important Goddess. But then, the addition of Xochiquetzal, Chantico, and Itzpapalotl was very welcome indeed, so I can't really grumble. Being something of a Mythology buff, I can vouch for the Four Tezcatlipocas being a thing. And Xochipilli would no doubt be the champion of the LGBT Rights movement in a modern setting. This one is a good one, guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T21:35:17-08:00","id":1010501,"title":"","content":"Hopefully Tlazolteotl can make her appearance in the Companion in the additional deities section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T21:37:47-08:00","id":1010502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1010419-pantheon-preview-the-teotl?p=1010499#post1010499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Xochipilli would no doubt be the champion of the LGBT Rights movement in a modern setting. This one is a good one, guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a character concept whose only major thing was &quot;DJ Teotl Scion&quot;. After reading the preview, that expanded to &quot;DJ Teotl who offers discount rates to LGBT clubs... And occasionally plays security there&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T22:29:35-08:00","id":1010523,"title":"","content":"The ability to play a Scion of what is essentially La Muerte, the goddess of death and creator of D\u00eda de Los Muertos...HELL YES!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T05:42:32-08:00","id":1010590,"title":"","content":"This was a really well-done preview! I echo Purple Snit in saying that I hope Tlazolteotl appears in the Companion, but honestly it's not that big a deal. We've already seen in the &quot;Missing Goddesses&quot; thread that it really isn't that hard for us to add other gods/goddesses in ourselves.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe big question I always have about the Teotl? The preview makes it clear that the other Pantheons don't approve of what the Teotl do. The Teotl, in turn, claim that what they do is necessary for the good of the world, and they tend to be pretty contemptuous of any Pantheon that isn't (in their mind) as willing to do whatever is necessary to protect the World. That's all well and good, but how does one lend credibility to the Teotl's argument? They claim that if they stop doing what they're doing, the Sun will die and there will be no other.<br /> <br /> \u200bWell? The other Pantheons can easily scoff at that idea and say &quot;Ummmm......you guys DO see that we've got no shortage of Sun Gods here in the Overworld, right? And that none of them need regular blood sacrifices to keep doing what they do, right?&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bHow should this argument be handled? If the Teotl are 100% right, then they are basically the only Pantheon that matters, and the other Pantheons should just shut up and let them do their thing. If the Teotl are 100% wrong, then the other Pantheons could literally just stand back and wait for them to die off and, in the minds of the other Pantheons, the World will be better off with one less Pantheon of savage blood gods.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat are some good ways to make this argument more than merely &quot;You're wrong! See? Here's proof!&quot; &quot;No, YOU'RE wrong!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T06:03:31-08:00","id":1010594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1010419-pantheon-preview-the-teotl?p=1010490#post1010490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't know, I'm open to the Old Man having found his way around all over western North America. It would definitely call for different Mantles in several cases though.<br /> <br /> (note: If he should have Beasts [Coyotes] he currently does not)</div> </div> </div> </div>I first read him AS Coyote, given that I know very little about him, and from what I do know, the old man seems very in his camp.<br /> <br /> given the very probably Mexica influences in western NA, I could see Coyote in those pantheons being The Old Man shouldering different mantles. It would be an interesting way to show how easily gods can straddle other pantheons within their proximities. Like how I assume Epona (given her reverance in more than a few different places in Europe) has mantles for the Romans, the Tuatha, and the Nemetondevos.<br /> <br /> other than spotting a couple typos and little grammatical things, I am loving what im seeing though. seems like a great step up from the Netjer preview. good job team!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8023,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","user":"Grimangel53","date":".  wanted to add a little thing. 12-01-2016, 09:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T06:27:19-08:00","id":1010602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1010419-pantheon-preview-the-teotl?p=1010590#post1010590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThe big question I always have about the Teotl? The preview makes it clear that the other Pantheons don't approve of what the Teotl do. The Teotl, in turn, claim that what they do is necessary for the good of the world, and they tend to be pretty contemptuous of any Pantheon that isn't (in their mind) as willing to do whatever is necessary to protect the World. That's all well and good, but how does one lend credibility to the Teotl's argument? They claim that if they stop doing what they're doing, the Sun will die and there will be no other.<br /> <br /> \u200bWell? The other Pantheons can easily scoff at that idea and say &quot;Ummmm......you guys DO see that we've got no shortage of Sun Gods here in the Overworld, right? And that none of them need regular blood sacrifices to keep doing what they do, right?&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bHow should this argument be handled? If the Teotl are 100% right, then they are basically the only Pantheon that matters, and the other Pantheons should just shut up and let them do their thing. If the Teotl are 100% wrong, then the other Pantheons could literally just stand back and wait for them to die off and, in the minds of the other Pantheons, the World will be better off with one less Pantheon of savage blood gods.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat are some good ways to make this argument more than merely &quot;You're wrong! See? Here's proof!&quot; &quot;No, YOU'RE wrong!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I normally make both sides of it absolutely true at the same time, and I also have the rest of the Pantheons not care for various reasons.<br /> <br /> So, the Teotl are absolutely correct that in order to continue supporting humanity through their various methods, be it carrying the sun, bringing rain, etc, they need blood sacrifices. If the sacrifices ever 100% totally stopped, The Fifth Sun is at a huge risk of ending, and requiring a recreation. (little cults have been providing what they can since the conquest) I extend this necessity to all Gods who are within a 'Teotl space', such as one of the many heavens. If you are a Deity, you need blood for the Aztec system. Now, other Pantheons when they are outside of the Aztec sphere of influence don't need this (and if the Teotl were in another Pantheon's 'place', they might not need to either. Most Pantheons keep to themselves however, it's an uncomfortable experience to have your existence as a Deity shift.) and instead have whatever limitations they have as part of their own culture.<br /> <br /> But, the biggest point is that other Pantheons don't care, with some exceptions. The Kami care because they're obsessively focused on blood as very much a bad thing. But, the rest of the Pantheons pretty much don't care. Partly because almost everyone has human sacrifice to some degree, or had it in the past, and partly because most Pantheons don't think mortals are people, just... things that are on earth being annoying.<br /> <br /> So, the way I deal with the arguing about who is right is that everyone is right, and the rest of the Pantheon's don't care. It doesn't make a huge amount of sense for them to care really. (I also have a bunch of other fluffy systems for different Pantheons going into other Pantheon's zones of influence. For example, a Deity in the Greek lands is 100% immortal, while a Deity in Ireland is frighteningly mortal)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T18:07:24-08:00","id":1011289,"title":"","content":"So no segment on their godrealm(s)? I know they mentioned a few by name in the god writeups, but I'd have appreciated a bit more specifically dedicated there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T22:44:27-08:00","id":1011380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1010419-pantheon-preview-the-teotl?p=1011289#post1011289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So no segment on their godrealm(s)? I know they mentioned a few by name in the god writeups, but I'd have appreciated a bit more specifically dedicated there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we've actually <i>had</i> a full pantheon writeup yet; it's just that previous ones have had a bit more info. I assume the Teotl's godrealms, Virtues, etc. will be in the full writeup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T08:18:52-08:00","id":1011504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1010419-pantheon-preview-the-teotl?p=1011380#post1011380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think we've actually <i>had</i> a full pantheon writeup yet; it's just that previous ones have had a bit more info. I assume the Teotl's godrealms, Virtues, etc. will be in the full writeup.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, you have - pantheon writeups are 7.5k apiece, so the Greek and Irish pantheons were complete. So was the Netjer, but, uh, they'll be revised a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T08:30:15-08:00","id":1011511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1010419-pantheon-preview-the-teotl?p=1011504#post1011504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, you have - pantheon writeups are 7.5k apiece, so the Greek and Irish pantheons were complete. So was the Netjer, but, uh, they'll be revised a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think I jumped to conclusions 'cause the Theoi and Tuatha didn't have any example Boons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T11:51:18-08:00","id":1011600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noneofyourbusiness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, the Theoi and Netjer writeups don't have example Titans, like the Tuatha writeup does.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They'll be expanded a bit to cover that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T12:05:13-08:00","id":1011604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1010419-pantheon-preview-the-teotl?p=1011504#post1011504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, you have - pantheon writeups are 7.5k apiece, so the Greek and Irish pantheons were complete. So was the Netjer, but, uh, they'll be revised a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does this work out then, since every Pantheon has their PSP and boons and two virtues along with the relevant fluff segment, but the previews we've seen so far don't all have those. I assumed the previewed PSPs and virtues would be in their own segment, maybe in the purviews chapter and virtues in the chargen zone. If they all add up to the total wordcount of the pantheon, every one of those previewed is going to need to be massaged to lose text from some areas and fit the others in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T12:39:55-08:00","id":1012110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> 